-- ============================================================================
-- H4 EXPERT DEEP SEED: Consequence Modelling, advanced tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, and the question rows from the
-- committed bank JSONs under tools/course-banks/consequence/advanced.
--
-- What this tier owns: WHO IS HURT, AND WHAT DOES THE ENGINE NOT KNOW. The
-- TNT equivalent mass as a single route quantity; cube root scaling and the
-- Kinney and Graham free air overpressure over a judged range, forward and
-- inverse; probits and the printed table; thermal probits and the four thirds,
-- with four presets named by source; the overpressure probit in psig; toxic
-- probits in two sources and two units, and a concentration that changes; the
-- dropped scope, the single route quantities and the approximate inverse
-- probit; and judgement from release to harm, with the seams to the Facilities
-- and quantitative risk courses. Digest sections 23 to 33, and section 34.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. Two presets can read one exposure as a few
-- percent or as most of the people exposed. The Expert capstone grades a
-- stated TNT mass forward and inverse and four probabilities, each on a
-- preset an independent published check stands behind, and no inverse of the
-- normal CDF.
-- ============================================================================

